sponding to the angle $\\theta =\\frac{14\\pi }{5}.$\n\nTo express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1**: Find the corresponding coterminal angle that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ We do this by subtracting integer multiples of $2\\pi $ until we get our desired angle.\n\n$$\n\\frac{14\\pi }{5}-2\\pi =\\frac{4\\pi }{5}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{5}).\n$$\n\n![](images/5e/5e1c95cc4e399b1902d230165341daa7388234b5edf7a64503f0007c34785242.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Compute the reference angle. Since $\\theta =\\frac{4\\pi }{5}$ is in the $2$nd quadrant, the reference angle is\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 3**: Determine the correct sign. The tangent function is negative $(-)$ in the second quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\n$$" 13194139538228 17592186576411 false] [17592186410424 1074 "We wish to express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{14\\pi }{5}\\right)$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ where ${\\theta }_{R}$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle $\\theta =\\frac{14\\pi }{5}.$\n\nTo express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{14\\pi }{5}\\right)$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1**: Find the corresponding coterminal angle that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ We do this by subtracting integer multiples of $2\\pi $ until we get our desired angle.\n\n$$\n\\frac{14\\pi }{5}-2\\pi =\\frac{4\\pi }{5}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{14\\pi }{5}\\right)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{4\\pi }{5}\\right).\n$$\n\n![]